// noxos-payload: Soong build file for the microdroid VM payload stub.
//
// Why Android.bp and not a standalone NDK/CMake project:
// AOSP's documented build path for a Microdroid VM payload
// (packages/modules/Virtualization/build/microdroid/README.md) is a
// cc_library_shared built with Soong inside the AOSP source tree, e.g.:
//
//   cc_library_shared {
//       name: "MyMicrodroidPayload",
//       srcs: ["**/*.cpp"],
//       sdk_version: "current",
//   }
//
// then embedded into a hosting app via jni_libs + use_embedded_native_libs
// in an android_app module. No official doc was found describing a
// supported standalone NDK/CMake build path for the payload binary itself
// (see README.md "Open questions" -- TODO verify in Phase 2).
//
// This module intentionally does NOT declare the android_app wrapper: the
// hosting app is noxos-app (a separate repo), out of scope here. This repo
// only owns the payload library and its config; wiring jni_libs / packaging
// assets/vm_config.json into an actual APK is noxos-app's job.
//
// shared_libs: ["libvm_payload#current"] is not shown in the README's
// trimmed example above, but was found referenced in an actual AOSP build
// diff for a real payload module.
//
// Confirmed against a real Soong build, 2026-09-15: the README's own
// sdk_version: "current" example (line 11 above) does NOT combine with
// shared_libs: ["libvm_payload#current"] - libvm_payload has no sdk-variant
// build, only a platform one, so sdk_version here produces a real
// "missing variant" Soong error. Deliberately omitted below, matching
// packages/modules/Virtualization/android/EmptyPayloadApp/Android.bp's
// MicrodroidEmptyPayloadJniLib - a real, working AOSP module with the exact
// same shared_libs dependency and no sdk_version on the native module
// (only on its wrapping android_app, which doesn't apply here since this
// repo has no app wrapper).
//
// Also confirmed 2026-09-15: shared_libs: ["libvm_payload#current"] alone is
// enough to make the real headers (vm_main.h, vm_payload.h) visible to a C++
// consumer - libvm_payload's own rust_ffi module declares
// include_dirs: ["include"], which Soong propagates to callers automatically.
// No header_libs needed here, matching EmptyPayloadApp/empty_binary.cpp (a
// real, working consumer with the same bare shared_libs dependency). The
// actual bug turned out to be in payload_main.cpp's own #include path, not
// here - see that file's history.

cc_library_shared {
    name: "noxos_payload_stub",
    stem: "libnoxos_payload_stub",
    srcs: [
        "payload_main.cpp",
        "exif_parser.cpp",
        "file_cheap_filter.cpp",
        "network_cheap_filter.cpp",
    ],
    shared_libs: [
        "libvm_payload#current",
    ],
    stl: "libc++_static",
}
